---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { issueChooserUrl, githubRepo } from '../../lib/contributions';
---
<Base title="Contribute" description="Help improve the public record of metro transit projects in India.">
  <div class="shell page-intro">
    <div class="section-label">CONTRIBUTE / PHASE 2</div>
    <h1>Help make the map <em>clearer.</em></h1>
    <p>Suggest a correction, add a source, or draw an approximate route. Reports are reviewed in the open before they change the public record.</p>
  </div>
  <section class="shell contribution-grid" aria-label="Ways to contribute">
    <article class="contribution-card"><span>01 / GEOGRAPHY</span><h2>Draw a route.</h2><p>Place dots on the city map to propose a line. Export GeoJSON and attach it to a new-project issue. With your permission and a merged PR, it can appear as a dashed, unverified community proposal.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/contribute/map/">Open route editor ↗</a></article>
    <article class="contribution-card"><span>02 / PROJECT FACTS</span><h2>Report an update.</h2><p>Share what changed, when it changed, and the source that supports it. A maintainer will review your report.</p>{issueChooserUrl ? <a class="button button-light" href={issueChooserUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open GitHub forms ↗</a> : <p class="contribution-setup">GitHub submission will be available after the public repository is connected.</p>}</article>
    <article class="contribution-card"><span>03 / DATA EDITS</span><h2>Send a pull request.</h2><p>Contributors comfortable with JSON can propose an edit directly. Read the review and source requirements first.</p><a class="text-link" href="/methodology/">Read methodology ↗</a></article>
  </section>
  <section class="shell contribution-process"><h2>How review works.</h2><ol><li>Submit a public report with a source.</li><li>A maintainer checks the claim and requests details if needed.</li><li>An accepted change is committed to the dataset and appears on the site after its next build.</li></ol><p>Reports and drawing drafts are proposals. A licensed route may be displayed after a reviewed merge, but it remains clearly marked unverified until its alignment is independently checked.</p>{githubRepo && <p>Public repository: <a href={`https://github.com/${githubRepo}`}>{githubRepo}</a>.</p>}</section>
</Base>
<style>
  .contribution-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:15px;padding-bottom:65px}.contribution-card{background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce5e4;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;min-height:245px;display:flex;flex-direction:column}.contribution-card>span{font-size:10px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#49a283}.contribution-card h2{font-size:23px;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:22px 0 8px}.contribution-card p,.contribution-process p{color:#667783;font-size:13px;line-height:1.65}.contribution-card a,.contribution-card .contribution-setup{margin-top:auto}.contribution-setup{font-size:11px;color:#687f81}.contribution-process{border-top:1px solid #dce5e4;padding-bottom:100px}.contribution-process h2{margin:32px 0 14px}.contribution-process ol{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:22px;padding-left:22px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}@media(max-width:750px){.contribution-grid,.contribution-process ol{grid-template-columns:1fr}.contribution-card{min-height:205px}}
</style>
